  "user_handle": "saraswati",
  "body": "# Finding Description and Impact\n`MonetrixVault.supplyToBlp()` registers a BLP supplied slot after sending action 15 without proving HyperCore activated the 0x811 slot. If the action is accepted but the slot remains unreadable, Accountant backing/surplus reads and settlement revert until cleanup.\n\n- No postcondition read is performed before `notifyVaultSupply`.\n- `sendSupply()` only forwards the raw borrow/lend action.\n- Every registered slot is later treated as an activated strict-read slot.\n\nThe Vault records the slot immediately after sending the action:\n```solidity\nActionEncoder.sendSupply(token, l1Amount);\nif (accountant != address(0)) {\n    uint32 perpIndex = 0;\n    if (token != uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX)) {\n        require(config.isSpotWhitelisted(uint32(token)), \"spot not whitelisted\");\n        perpIndex = config.spotToPerp(uint32(token));\n    }\n    MonetrixAccountant(accountant).notifyVaultSupply(token, perpIndex);\n}\nemit BlpSupplied(token, l1Amount);\n```\n\nThe action encoder only forwards the raw action:\n```solidity\nfunction sendSupply(uint64 token, uint64 l1Amount) internal {\n    bytes memory action = abi.encodePacked(\n        HyperCoreConstants.ACTION_VERSION,\n        HyperCoreConstants.ACTION_BORROW_LEND,\n        abi.encode(uint8(0), token, l1Amount)\n    );\n    _sendRaw(action);\n}\n```\n\nAccountant backing reads strictly dereference each registered slot:\n```solidity\nuint256 slen = suppliedList.length;\nfor (uint256 i = 0; i < slen; i++) {\n    SuppliedAsset storage a = suppliedList[i];\n    if (a.spotToken == uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX)) {\n        total += int256(PrecompileReader.suppliedUsdcEvm(account));\n    } else {\n        total += int256(\n            PrecompileReader.suppliedNotionalUsdcFromPerp(uint32(a.spotToken), a.perpIndex, account)\n        );\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### **Exploit Path**\n1. The Vault has an Accountant configured and no active registration for the target BLP slot.\n2. The operator calls `supplyToBlp`; the EVM CoreWriter call succeeds, but HyperCore leaves the 0x811 supplied-balance slot inactive.\n3. The Vault still calls `notifyVaultSupply`, adding that token to `vaultSupplied`.\n4. Later `totalBackingSigned()`, `distributableSurplus()`, and `settleDailyPnL()` revert until `removeSuppliedEntry` clears it.\n\n### **Impact**\n- Yield settlement is blocked because Gate 3 needs a successful `distributableSurplus()` calculation.\n- Vault backing/surplus accounting and monitoring are unavailable while the stale slot remains registered.\n\nBecause this causes the stated Medium impact, this warrants the selected severity.\n\n### **Recommended Mitigation Steps**\n- In `MonetrixVault.supplyToBlp()`, call `notifyVaultSupply` only after verifying the supplied slot is readable and active.\n- If HyperCore activation can be asynchronous, use pending registration and promote it only after a successful `suppliedBalance` read.\n- Keep `removeSuppliedEntry` as repair, but do not rely on it to prevent bad registrations.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.28;\n\nimport \"../simulator/SimulatorBase.sol\";\n\ncontract BlpSupplyStaleRegistrationPoC is SimulatorBase {\n    function setUp() public {\n        setUpSimulator();\n    }\n\n    function testSupplyRegistersSlotEvenWhenHyperCoreDoesNotActivateIt() public {\n        bytes memory suppliedRead = abi.encode(address(vault), USDC_TOKEN);\n        vm.mockCallRevert(\n            HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_SUPPLIED_BALANCE,\n            suppliedRead,\n            \"BLP supply slot never activated\"\n        );\n\n        // Setup: no registered slot means backing skips the strict 0x811 read.\n        assertEq(accountant.vaultSuppliedLength(), 0);\n        accountant.totalBackingSigned();\n\n        // Trigger: action 15 is accepted, but no supplied balance is activated.\n        vm.prank(operator);\n        vault.supplyToBlp(USDC_TOKEN, 1_000_000);\n\n        assertEq(accountant.vaultSuppliedLength(), 1);\n        (uint64 spotToken, uint32 perpIndex) = accountant.vaultSupplied(0);\n        assertEq(spotToken, USDC_TOKEN);\n        assertEq(perpIndex, 0);\n\n        // Proof: the stale registration now breaks all strict backing reads.\n        vm.expectRevert(bytes(\"PrecompileReader: supplied balance read failed\"));\n        accountant.totalBackingSigned();\n    }\n}\n```",
